    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 142</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_142/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 25 Dec 2024 00:24:33 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_142/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;What is the output of the following code?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;package main&#xA;&#xA;import &amp;#34;fmt&amp;#34;&#xA;&#xA;func main() {&#xA;       var s map[string]int&#xA;       delete(s, &amp;#34;h&amp;#34;)&#xA;       fmt.Println(s[&amp;#34;h&amp;#34;])&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;A. runtime panic&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;B. 0&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;C. compilation error&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;B&#xA;&lt;a href=&#34;https://go.dev/play/p/rfK0pIKBRRx&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;external nofollow noopener noreferrer&#34;&gt;Run online&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Using &lt;code&gt;delete&lt;/code&gt; on an uninitialized map (not made with &lt;code&gt;make&lt;/code&gt;) will not cause an error.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Accessing an uninitialized map returns the zero value corresponding to the value type.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h4 class=&#34;heading-element&#34; id=&#34;extension&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;Extension&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;a href=&#34;#extension&#34; class=&#34;heading-mark&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;svg class=&#34;octicon octicon-link&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 16 16&#34; version=&#34;1.1&#34; width=&#34;16&#34; height=&#34;16&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;Assigning to an uninitialized map will cause a panic.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 141</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_141/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 25 Dec 2024 00:09:11 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_141/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;What is the output of the following code?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;func main() {&#xA;    s := make(map[string]int)&#xA;    delete(s, &amp;#34;h&amp;#34;)&#xA;    fmt.Println(s[&amp;#34;h&amp;#34;])&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;A. runtime panic&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;B. 0&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;C. compilation error&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;B&#xA;&lt;a href=&#34;https://go.dev/play/p/uvHvPF8EdU-&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;external nofollow noopener noreferrer&#34;&gt;Run online&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;Deleting a non-existent key does not cause a panic.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h4 class=&#34;heading-element&#34; id=&#34;extended-question&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;Extended Question&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;a href=&#34;#extended-question&#34; class=&#34;heading-mark&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;svg class=&#34;octicon octicon-link&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 16 16&#34; version=&#34;1.1&#34; width=&#34;16&#34; height=&#34;16&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;p&gt;In this problem, &lt;code&gt;s&lt;/code&gt; is already initialized. Would the behavior be the same if it were uninitialized?&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 105</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_105/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 06 Dec 2024 23:42:44 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_105/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;What is the output value of &lt;code&gt;counter&lt;/code&gt; in the following code?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;func main() {&#xA;    var m = map[string]int{&#xA;        &amp;#34;A&amp;#34;: 21,&#xA;        &amp;#34;B&amp;#34;: 22,&#xA;        &amp;#34;C&amp;#34;: 23,&#xA;    }&#xA;    counter := 0&#xA;    for k, v := range m {&#xA;        if counter == 0 {&#xA;            delete(m, &amp;#34;A&amp;#34;)&#xA;        }&#xA;        counter&amp;#43;&amp;#43;&#xA;        fmt.Println(k, v)&#xA;    }&#xA;    fmt.Println(&amp;#34;counter is &amp;#34;, counter)&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;A. 2&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;B. 3&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;C. 2 or 3&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;C&#xA;Maps are reference types and will affect the original map.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 050</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_050/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 06 Dec 2024 20:44:29 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_050/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;What is the output of the following code?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;func main() {  &#xA;    s := make(map[string]int)&#xA;    delete(s, &amp;#34;h&amp;#34;)&#xA;    fmt.Println(s[&amp;#34;h&amp;#34;])&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;A. runtime panic&#xA;B. 0&#xA;C. compilation error&#xA;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;B 0&#xA;Deleting a non-existent key will not cause a panic.&#xA;Outputting a non-existent key will return the zero value of its type.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Extension:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;func main() {&#xA;    var s map[string]int&#xA;    delete(s, &amp;#34;h&amp;#34;)&#xA;    s[&amp;#34;h&amp;#34;] = 1&#xA;    fmt.Println(s[&amp;#34;h&amp;#34;])&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p&gt;Deleting from a nil map will also not panic.&#xA;However, writing to a nil map will panic.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
